            "bio": "Johary RAJOSEFA has held the position of General Project Coordinator since 2019. Despite the pandemic, he has strongly contributed to the implementation of various structuring and innovative projects in Madagascar in the field of Tourism and Transport, the reopening of Malagasy borders in good sanitary conditions as well as to the revival of the Tourism sector which has been undermined by the global health crisis.\n\nCurrently, its mission is focused on promoting and facilitating investments in the tourism sector, particularly in the development of the hospitality industry. This is one of the conditions to achieve the Malagasy government's target of crossing the million-tourist mark in 2028. He will draw on his 11 years of experience as part of the executive team of the Economic Development Board of Madagascar (EDBM), the national investment promotion agency (IPA), to lead to the implementation of investment projects that will maximize Madagascar's benefits and have strong positive impacts within local communities.\n",
