            "firstname": "David",
            "email": "david@oraculi.co",
            "company": "ōrāculī",
            "lastname": "Singleton",
            "title": "Founder",
            "bio": "Talks about: #Leadership #BrandDevelopment #TransformationalGrowthCoach #F&B #Franchise #StrategicAdvisory #Oraculi #AI #NonExecutive #PrivateEquity #Coaching #PersonalDevelopment #ProfessionalDevelopment\n\nDavid has led and developed organisations around the world working with some of the world's best known and loved brands in 40 countries. He now works as a strategic advisor to brands, organisations, teams and ambitious senior executives in growth mode. \n\nAs an accredited leadership coach, he works as a transformational growth coach with c suite leaders, ambitious senior leaders and teams on their quest to be the best versions of themselves and the best business in their class. \n\nDavid’s hospitality career began in the UK where he led and developed F&B brands across the country including America leading a franchise team on his first brand to the UK. Whilst there he studied and researched at the University of Central Florida. He attained his Masters degree at Coventry University where he was subsequently invited to join their Advisory Board until he left the UK to embark on his International career in Moscow where he worked as part of a board level turnaround team for Russia and the CIS largest restaurant group as Brand Director and then as a consultant designer for Mercedes Benz creating their first restaurant of its kind to enable the launch of the A Class into Russia. \n\nHe moved to the UAE to take a position on the Retail Board of Al Tayer as Vice President responsible for 15 restaurant brands across the region and then took responsibility for the franchised Hard Rock Café business across 40 countries in EMEA and South Asia as Vice President.  \n\nHard Rock was David’s last corporate role in global boardrooms before establishing his boutique advisory firm and in 2022 formed Oraculi his thought leadership and strategic advisory practice which he now leads as founder, advisor, NED, and transformational growth coach and business mentor.  \n\nDavid has widened his expertise from a focused hospitality and F&B position where he is widely regarded as a subject matter expert, in particular from a franchise perspective. His advisory roles now include AI technology, brand development and design, largescale events, consumer brand and a significant non-executive role in a private equity venture. His pro bono roles include a board role with the British Business Group, the largest such business networking group in the region and ranked in the top three Chambers in the world.    \n\nOraculi is the Latin interpretation ‘to mentor’, the central purpose to David’s work whether he is coaching, advising or developing. David’s accredited coaching practice focuses on leading through change and transformation. Senior leaders operate at the confluence of delivering the bottom line and simultaneously transforming the business. In today’s hyper-connected business environment leaders face many disruptive challenges environmental, social, regulators, the press and much more. David’s coaching practice focuses on helping leaders navigate time horizons and fuel personal and professional development.\n\nDavid is an Elite speaker with Elevate.ac. Elevate was formed by Robert Clarke, former entrepreneur in residence at the University of Central Florida and reached out to David to ask for his advice and support to create an affordable masterclass.com which has now a subscription based platform with more than 300 inspirational speakers, thought leaders and coaches. David regularly speaks and shares his coaching inspiration globally via Elevate.\n\nDavid has two daughters who both live and work in Dubai; Katie a teacher and Hollie who is a Marketing and PR Manager. \n\n\n",
