            "bio": "A hotelier by excellence, with over 21 years of well-rounded experience that truly sets Ahmed apart.\n\nHis exceptional leadership skills and genuine care for his team members, fostering a collaborative and supportive work environment that encourages growth and success.\n\nThroughout his career. Ahmed worked with renown owners, developers, operators, and advisors, including IHG, Hyatt, Sun International, Moevenpick, Millennium, Accor, and Kempinski. His expertise spans hotel operations, corporate roles, project management, project development, and advisory services.\n\nHe has a unique ability to unite his team around a common goal, driving projects to completion with dedication and enthusiasm.\n\nAhmed has efficiently managed 9 pre-openings, 2 rebranding, and over 2 new builds.\n\nComes to count an additional 35 refurbishment projects with several design reviews and valuable input into international summit and conferences.\n\nAhmed is an active member in supporting operational and sustainable development through his contribution as an advisory board member in the first RAK Energy Summit in Ras Al Khaimah and in the development committee of the sustainability regulation of the Emirate of Ras Al Khaimah (Barjeel) .\n\nWith an outstanding financial knowledge and extensive expertise in design and construction contracting, particularly with FIDIC forms of contracts, set him apart in the industry.\n\nAhmed's experience expands beyond hotels to adventure tourism, where he led the developments of the Jais Sledder and Bear Grylls Explorers’ Camp. His diverse skill set makes him a valuable resource for any organization in the hospitality and tourism sectors.",
